# ⚠ THE TWO BELOW ARE REQUIRED BY THE FLAG ABOVE AND WERE DOCUMENTED NOWHERE (W6.23).
# cmd/lens/attestation_wiring.go reads both directly; with either missing the verify
# sweep logs "sweep stays inert (no pinned root to verify against)" and does nothing.
# So the flag above was discoverable and the two things it needs were not: following
# the documentation enabled a security feature that then silently did not run.
# LENS_NVIDIA_ROOT_CA_PEM=   # PEM of the pinned NVIDIA attestation root CA
# LENS_NVIDIA_JWKS_URL=      # JWKS endpoint the attestation verifier fetches keys from
# LENS_NODE_AUTOROUTE_ENABLED=
# LENS_NODE_LATENCY_CAPTURE_ENABLED=
# LENS_NODE_PRIVATE_CIDR_ALLOWLIST=
# LENS_NODE_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=
# LENS_OBS_WRITE_MAX_CONCURRENT=
# LENS_OPERATOR_ALERT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_OPERATOR_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# LENS_PATTERN_CAPTURE_ENABLED=
# LENS_PATTERN_CONCENTRATION_VELOCITY_MAX=
# LENS_PATTERN_EARNING_ENABLED=
# LENS_PATTERN_EARN_CAP_PER_WORKSPACE=
# LENS_PATTERN_EARN_CAP_WINDOW=
# LENS_PATTERN_MINING_ENABLED=
# Cross-tenant pooling SHADOW LOG (W4.9): post-serve, void, fingerprint-only record of what WOULD
# have pooled, so the pooled hit rate is measurable on real traffic while pooling stays OFF. It
# writes no prompt text and cannot serve, pool or mint. Read back with poolshadow.Recorder.Rate;
# see migrations/0125_pooled_shadow_observations.sql. Default false.
# LENS_POOL_SHADOW_LOG_ENABLED=
# Consumer discount on CROSS-TENANT POOLED cache hits (r, default 0.30, must be in [0,1)).
# A pooled hit costs Talyvor no provider call, so the whole charge is margin; this hands r of it
# back to the consumer. The contributor's royalty is a share of the DISCOUNTED charge, so raising r
# reduces contributor earnings by the same fraction. r=0 restores the old behaviour (charge list).
# LENS_POOL_CONSUMER_DISCOUNT=
# LENS_POOL_HOLDBACK_WINDOW=
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_PER_ENTRY=
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_PER_PAIR=
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_WINDOW=
# LENS_POOL_ROYALTY_MINTING_ENABLED=
# LENS_POOL_ROYALTY_SHARE=
# LENS_POVI_CHALLENGE_KEY=
# LENS_POVI_CHALLENGE_RATE=
# LENS_POVI_MINTING_ENABLED=
# LENS_POVI_MIN_STAKE=
# LENS_POVI_SLASH_FRACTION=
# LENS_POVI_UNBOND_PERIOD=
# LENS_PROOF_OF_BENCHMARK_ENABLED=
# LENS_PROOF_OF_IMPROVEMENT_ENABLED=
# LENS_PROVISION_SECRET=
# LENS_REDIS_TLS=
# LENS_REDIS_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=
# LENS_REPUTATION_BONDED_MINTING_ENABLED=
# LENS_RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY=
# LENS_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=
# LENS_RETRY_MAX_DELAY=
# LENS_ROI_INCLUDE_ENGINEER_BREAKDOWN=
# LENS_ROUTING_BRAIN_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_DECISION_CAPTURE_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_MINTING_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_RATE_PER_POINT=
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_SCORING_ENABLED=
# LENS_ROUTING_TIER_COHORTS_ENABLED=
# LENS_SEMANTIC_CACHE_RETENTION=
# LENS_SEMANTIC_CACHE_SWEEP_INTERVAL=
# LENS_SETTLEMENT_FAIL_CLOSED_ENABLED=
# LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# LENS_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# W6.10 — PROVIDER-SECRET ENVELOPE KEK: the key that wraps CUSTOMER provider
# credentials (BYOK). One or more base64 32-byte keys, comma separated, PRIMARY
# FIRST — generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`. Unset ⇒ Lens boots with
# provider-secret custody DISABLED and there is no plaintext fallback; set to
# anything that is not exactly 32 decoded bytes ⇒ Lens refuses to boot, naming
# this variable. To rotate, PREPEND the new key and keep the old one listed until
# a rewrap pass has moved every row.
# ⚠ LOSE THIS KEY AND EVERY STORED PROVIDER SECRET IS UNRECOVERABLE. There is no
# escrow and no Talyvor-side copy — that is the property, not an oversight.
# Recovery is re-entry by the customer. See docs/provider-secret-envelope.md.
# LENS_PROVIDER_SECRET_KEK=
# W4.6.1 step 4 — SESSION-SCOPED KEYS: the credential a browser chat holds instead
# of a workspace API key. OFF by default; off means the three /v1/auth/session-keys
# routes are never registered (a 404, not a route that refuses) and every tlv_sk_
# bearer is refused, so an unconfigured deployment is unchanged by the feature.
# LENS_SESSION_KEYS_ENABLED=
# The CEILING on a minted session key's life (Go duration, e.g. 45m). Default 1h,
# hard maximum 12h — a value above that is REFUSED at startup rather than clamped,
# so this file cannot disagree with the running process. It is a ceiling, not the
# lifetime: the actual TTL is min(what the caller asked for, this, the caller's own
# remaining sign-in), and the third bound is the one that makes it a session key.
# LENS_SESSION_KEY_TTL=
# LENS_SUBSCRIPTION_ALLOWANCE_ULXC=
# LENS_SYNTHETIC_KEY=
# B19.16 — agent approvals signed with the owner's passkey, and a web push per approval filed.
# Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example); `lens vapid-key` makes a VAPID key.
# LENS_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# LENS_VAPID_SUBJECT=
# LENS_WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS=
# LENS_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=
# B40.4 — the phone app's device keys. Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_DEVICE_APPLE_APP_ID=
# LENS_DEVICE_TEST_ATTESTATION=
# B40.10 — speech (/v1/audio/*). Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# LENS_DEEPGRAM_URL=

# B20.2 — the buyers' monthly marketplace bill (a Stripe metered price and its meter's event name).
# Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_MARKET_BILL_PRICE_ID=
# LENS_MARKET_METER_EVENT=
# B32.39 — each billed use's tax, its own line on the same bill (a second metered price and its meter's event name,
# and the test-mode twin's price). Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_MARKET_TAX_PRICE_ID=
# LENS_MARKET_TAX_METER_EVENT=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_MARKET_TAX_PRICE_ID=
# B32.45 — who works out the tax on Talyvor's own sales: test (the tax rows) or stripe (Stripe Tax, test mode).
# LENS_TAX_PARTNER=test
# B32.40 — the supplier on Talyvor's marketplace receipts: its name, address and VAT number (empty: every receipt reads
# "VAT registration pending" and is a Preview). Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_SUPPLIER_LEGAL_NAME=
# LENS_SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# LENS_SUPPLIER_VAT_NUMBER=
# B32.21 — the most free trial uses one per_use offer may give each buyer (default 5). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_MARKET_TRIAL_MAX=
# B32.24 — the largest remix share a royalty listing may ask (default 3000 bps) and how many generations the
# lineage read walks (default 5). Set them in lens.env.
# LENS_LINEAGE_MAX_SHARE_BPS=
# LENS_LINEAGE_MAX_DEPTH=
# B32.26 — the most a listing's parents together receive of what it received from a sale (default 5000 bps). Set it
# in lens.env.
# LENS_LINEAGE_TOTAL_CAP_BPS=
# B32.46 — how similar a new listing version may be to another seller's listing it does not declare as a parent before
# it is held for review (default 0.92). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_MARKET_SIMILARITY_HOLD=
# B32.47 — how many days a seller has to counter an IP claim against their listing (default 10). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_IP_COUNTER_DAYS=
# B32.41 — the days between the requests to a seller with earnings for their tax details; the third holds their payouts
# until they are complete (default 30). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_SELLER_TAX_REMINDER_DAYS=
# B32.42 — the day of the week, UTC, sellers are paid on: MON to SUN (default MON). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_WEEKDAY=
# B32.43 — whether a self-billing seller's VAT is worked out and paid with their payout (default false: every
# self-billed invoice at zero VAT, "VAT on your supply: under review"). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_SELF_BILLING_VAT=
# B32.30 — how many messages one member posts in one room in a minute (default 20). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_ROOM_MESSAGES_PER_MINUTE=
# B32.33 — how many of a room's latest messages its AI reads with a member's question (default 30). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_ROOM_CONTEXT_MESSAGES=
# B32.52 — how many workspaces' open reports take a public room off the list until it is reviewed (default 3). Set it in lens.env.
# LENS_ROOM_REPORTS_HIDE=
# B30.5 — Know Your Agent: the Ed25519 key agent credentials are signed with (base64 of a 32-byte seed; unset, one is
# made each start), and how long a credential is valid (default 24h). Set them in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_KYA_SIGNING_KEY=
# LENS_KYA_CREDENTIAL_TTL=
# B30.112 — Persona's API key and "KYC" inquiry template (a person's identity, L2) and a Companies House REST API key
# (a UK company, L3); empty keeps the Test provider. Set them in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_PERSONA_API_KEY=
# LENS_PERSONA_TEMPLATE_ID=
# LENS_COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY=
# B30.6 — how similar a name must be to one on a sanctions list for its payee or payment to be held for an operator,
# 0 to 1 (Nicolai sets it; default 0.9). Set it in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_SCREENING_FUZZY_THRESHOLD=
# B37.4 — how many hours old a sanctions list may get before every payment in or out is held for an operator
# (Nicolai sets it; default 48). Set it in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_SCREENING_MAX_AGE_HOURS=
# B19.12 — agent cards (test mode only): the Stripe Issuing real-time authorisation endpoint's signing
# secret, and the currency cards are issued in. Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_STRIPE_ISSUING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_STRIPE_ISSUING_CURRENCY=
# B25.2 — test (synthetic) users pay in Stripe test mode: the test-mode key, the signing secret of the
# /v1/billing/webhook/test endpoint, and the test-mode plans and (B25.6) marketplace bill price. Set these
# in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_MARKET_BILL_PRICE_ID=
# B20.5 — where Stripe's seller onboarding returns to. Set these in lens.env (see lens.env.example).
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_RETURN_URL=
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_REFRESH_URL=
# LENS_TLS_CACHE_DIR=
# LENS_TLS_DOMAIN=
# LENS_TOKEN_TTL=
# LENS_TRACK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_TRACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# LENS_TRUSTFUL_COMPUTE_MINT_ENABLED=
# LENS_WORKSPACE_MAX_STALENESS=
# LENS_WORKSPACE_RELOAD_INTERVAL=
# LENS_WORKTIER_ENABLED=
# LENS_SHADOW_MINTS_ENABLED=

# ── developer / check tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by cmd/lens's `canoncheck` subcommand only; never by the serving path.
# Documented here because W6.23's census asserts that every LENS_* name the
# binary reads appears in a shipped artefact, and "it is only a dev tool" is a
# reason to write down, not a reason to omit.
# LENS_CANON_MODEL=
